From 488eb8cede6b7e13316133e079abcdc8b714f404 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 16:23:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08468/11362] [outer-loop] ARC levers #3+#4: expand live-path
 budgets for Kaggle-class hardware; fix exp6091 truncation

Operator directive 2026-08-07 (ops/known-issues.md): the scored eval GPU is far
faster/bigger than local dev hardware, so budgets sized for local wall-clock
under-use the eval envelope.

Lever #3 (arc_competition_agent.py, scripts/kaggle/submission_kernel/main.py):
- CarnotAgent.MAX_ACTIONS 400 -> 2000. Evidence:
  results/outer_loop_scored_path_budget_sweep_20260726.json (25 games x 3
  seeds, LLM-off) -- median wins climb 4@400 -> 9@1000 -> 11@2000 -> 12@4000,
  no saturation. 2000 captures 11 of the 12-win ceiling while staying near the
  artifact's conservative worst-case-safe-host-RAM neighborhood (real host RAM
  on the actual Kaggle machine is still unmeasured).
- SUBMITTED_TARGET_LEVELS 3 -> 8 (the next binding give-up cap once actions
  are no longer the constraint).
- SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE None -> 400 (pure wall/memory savings; the
  post-solve tail scores 0 either way).
- Kernel env: CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_MAX_TOKENS 4096->8192,
  CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_TIMEOUT 600->1200, scored-run-only via setdefault (local
  LocalGGUFProposer default of 4096/600 is untouched, still pinned by
  test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py). The kernel's own VRAM-fit check warns
  (does not abort) if the attached card can't hold the raised n_ctx.

Lever #4 (scripts/experiments/outer_loop_arc_refine_engine_visible_ab_20260803.py):
- BUDGET default 4096 -> 16384, the value the successful 2026-08-06 24-cell
  run used (commit 787594eb68 traced the original truncation). One line
  covers all three A/B arms identically (single shared LocalGGUFProposer),
  preserving the arms-differ-in-exactly-one-thing invariant. Launched a
  background resume run to complete the 2 missing cells (cd82 trial 1, sk48
  trial 1) at the now-permanent budget.

Verification: all three source files py_compile clean. Targeted test sweep (7
files, 89 tests via --no-cov) has exactly 1 failure
(test_experiment_4754_submitted_agent_config.py::test_scenario_arc_wmte_4754_run_writes_artifact_and_blocks),
confirmed PRE-EXISTING via git-stash isolation (fails identically with these
changes fully stashed out) -- unrelated to this change.

Artifact-freshness gate: this file is a registered dependency of 11 analyser
artifacts (arc_gateway_card_ground_truth, arc_per_level_reset_attribution,
experiment_6011/6012/6013, outer_loop_arc_{reset_charge_attribution,
gateway_rescore, first_win_llm_on_eval_concurrency, early_stop_grace_sweep,
generator_concurrency_fix, llm_on_wallclock_envelope}). Each was individually
checked against its own generating script for genuine relevance (not a
blanket wave-through): most reference none of the three changed symbols or
explicitly hold them out of scope; two artifacts (early_stop_grace_sweep,
llm_on_wallclock_envelope) record a "not yet flipped / MAX_ACTIONS still 400"
status note that this exact commit is the authorized event superseding --
their underlying swept-value measurements (gathered via explicit parameter
injection, not the live default) are unaffected. Acknowledgements added per
scripts/artifact_freshness_lint.py's documented schema (path/sha256_was/
sha256_now/reason/evidence, pinned to the exact new hash so the next edit
re-trips the lint). One second-order cascade
(outer_loop_arc_gateway_accurate_rescore_20260726.json, which cites two of
the above artifacts BY HASH) acknowledged the same way -- metadata-only
change, no cited number moved. artifact-freshness-lint: OK.

